Z||000003||frontal lobe||03-13-2000||10:52 PM||||Oreif,  <BR>Clearance from the wife already obtained.  Time of departure set.  Gas tank full.  Directions printed out.  I'll try to find you there.  How will I know it's you?  You wouldn't mind face painting the fiero logo on your cheek so I could pick you out, would you?  As far as joining, I live in southern Wisconsin now, but I graduated from high school in Freeport (northern Ill.), does that count??||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||03-14-2000||02:44 AM||||Peoria to Barrington Illinois is probably a 4 hour drive. His address is:<BR>7 Hillside drive Unit 3<BR>Barrington IL 60010<BR>The time is 1pm<BR>His phone is 847-304-4480<BR>He is going to show how a V-8 goes into a Fiero, His new body kits, How to chop the top of the Fiero, And other stuff.<BR>Frontal Lobe, We have people from all over the country in our club including people outside of our country! Anyone can join. As for finding me, I'll be the one who didn't drive his Fiero. (it's in the garage getting a whole new suspension) I will be driving my metallic grey Saturn. Also I will have a very tired look, Going with a friend very early in the morning to pick up a Fiero GT he bought. It's about 2 hours south of us and we'll be leaving around 4am so we can be back by 9am. Did I mention I work nights? So off at midnight, quick nap, Long drive, quick nap then to Archies!<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-14-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||Oreif||03-14-2000||02:55 AM||||sloponti, Here's directions from Yahoo numbers at the end of each is miles on that road. <BR>1. Start out going South on US-24 W/IL-29 S towards HAMILTON BLVD by turning left. 0.2 <BR>2. Take the I-74 EAST ramp towards BLOOMINGTON. 0.1 <BR>3. Merge onto I-74 E. 33.5 <BR>4. Take the I-55 NORTH exit 0.6 <BR>5. Merge onto I-55 N. 105.7 <BR>6. Take the exit 0.5 <BR>7. Take the I-355 NORTH exit towards WEST SUBURBS. 0.9 <BR>8. Stay straight to go onto N SOUTH TOLLWAY (Portions toll). 9.2 <BR>9. Take the IL-56/BUTTERFIELD RD exit. 0.3 <BR>10. Merge onto I-355 NORTH RAMP. 0.9 <BR>11. Merge onto N SOUTH TOLLWAY (Portions toll). 6.6 <BR>12. N SOUTH TOLLWAY becomes I-355 N. 2.4 <BR>13. I-355 N becomes I-290 W. 5.6 <BR>14. Take I-90 RAMP towards ROCKFORD/CHICAGO(I-90)/ALGONQUIN RD(IL-62). 1.8 <BR>15. Merge onto IL-53 N. 0.5 <BR>16. Take the KIRCHOFF RD exit. 0.2 <BR>17. Turn LEFT onto W KIRCHOFF RD. 0.2 <BR>18. Turn RIGHT onto HICKS RD. 1.6 <BR>19. Turn LEFT onto S HICKS RD/E NORTHWEST HWY/US-14. 0.9 <BR>20. S HICKS RD/E NORTHWEST HWY/US-14 becomes E BALDWIN RD/E NORTHWEST HWY/US-14 W. 0.5 <BR>21. E BALDWIN RD/E NORTHWEST HWY/US-14 W becomes W NORTHWEST HWY/US-14. 9.4 <BR>22. Turn RIGHT onto HILLVIEW DR. 0.1 <BR>23. Turn RIGHT onto HILLSIDE DR. 0.0 <P>Yahoo says it should take 218 minutes. So figure 3.5 hours drive time.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Richard Parnell||03-15-2000||02:00 PM||||Man, I wish I could go.  If anyone makes a video of the goings on I'd pay for the tape, time, and postage.  I'm so sick of being stuck here in Hawaii.  It's not as cool as people think.  Lousy/few roads and way too many drivers.  Now to top it all off the only road around Ohahu has been blocked by the state because a few boulders fell at Waimea Bay.  I can either drive around the island to work (2 hours) which is usually a 15-20 minute drive.  Or I can bus it to the bay and hike across the beach.  Then take my car which I've left over at the park (I'm weirded out leaving my little baby all alone over there at night).  Now a bunch of obstructionist idiot hawaiian activists are preventing the road from being fixed by saying the gods are upset that we've disturbed them with whatever.  It's nuts, beam me out Scottie.||||reg||9
Z||000007||frontal lobe||03-16-2000||12:20 AM||||That is SO like a hawaiian god isn't it?  You know, they could have erupted a volcano, started a massive tidal wave but no, they have to drop a couple boulders on a road.  Those activists really know how to read the signs, don't they?||||reg||1
